This copy is a test program of lean2rr. We changed these files:

- lean-toolchain: leanprover/lean4:v4.34.0 (upstream: v4.8.0-rc1).
  lean2rr reads the .olean files of Lean 4.34.0, so the program must
  build with that version.
- Main.lean: `Array.mkArray` became `Array.replicate`. Lean 4.34 does
  not have `Array.mkArray`.
- Main.lean: `writeTestImage` takes the width, the samples per pixel,
  the number of threads and the maximum depth as parameters. Their
  defaults are the upstream values. `main` reads them from the command
  line: `render FILE WIDTH SAMPLES THREADS [DEPTH]`. Thus the test can
  render small images.
- Main.lean: THREADS = 0 renders on the main thread, without a task.
  The divisor of the pixel sums is then the samples per pixel. All tasks
  take random numbers from the same generator, IO.stdGenRef. With two or
  more tasks, the image thus depends on the order in which the threads
  run. Only THREADS = 0 and THREADS = 1 give one image that the test can
  compare.
- Main.lean: a note at the top and two comments say what changed.

Render/Vec3.lean, lakefile.lean, lake-manifest.json and LICENSE.md are
unchanged. We did not copy c/ (a C version of the program), old/ (older
files that the program does not use), output/ (images), README.md and
.gitignore.
